irgsh (2.0.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Add multi-distribution support: chief is now distribution-agnostic and
    routes tasks by dist to per-distribution Machinery queues
    (irgsh-<dist_codename>), replacing the single shared "irgsh" queue
  * BREAKING: builder and iso now require a dist_codename in their config;
    irgsh-cli requires --dist on `package submit` and `livebuild submit`,
    and --repo-dist on `import` (existing --dist there still means the
    source suite)
  * BREAKING: wire format for Submission/ISOSubmission gains a required
    dist field; ImportSubmission gains targetDist
  * Config validation is now scoped per component (its own section plus
    redis: only), so e.g. irgsh-repo no longer requires chief:/builder:
    to be populated in its config file
  * Convert the default install flow (make build-install/install.sh) from
    sysv init scripts to native systemd units, matching how the Debian
    package has always installed them
  * Add dist/target_dist columns to the jobs, iso_jobs and import_jobs
    SQLite tables (migrated automatically on existing databases)

